  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1406.05 Offsite Shipments",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1406.05 Offsite Shipments.\n\n(a) Except as provided in (c) and (d), below, a used oil generator, household DIY used oil collection center, commercial used oil collection center, or used oil aggregation point shall ensure that its used oil is transported only by a used oil transporter that possesses an EPA identification number and a current and valid New Hampshire hazardous waste transporter registration.\n\n(b) If a shipment of used oil subject to regulation under this chapter is accompanied by a manifest, the NH01 hazardous waste number shall not be recorded on the manifest.\n\n(c) Subject to the requirements of (d), below, a used oil generator, household DIY used oil collection center, or used oil aggregation point may self-transport the following, without obtaining an EPA identification number and a current and valid New Hampshire hazardous waste transporter registration:\n\n(1) Used oil that is generated at the generator’s site;\n\n(2) Used oil received while acting as a used oil aggregation point; and\n\n(3) Household DIY used oil received from household DIY used oil generators.\n\n(d) For purposes of (c), above, the used oil shall be transported:\n\n(1) In a vehicle owned by the generator, household DIY used oil collection center, or used oil aggregation point, or an employee thereof;\n\n(2) In quantities of no more than 55 gallons of used oil at any time;\n\n(3) In containers that meet US DOT specifications for hazardous materials under 49 CFR 173; and\n\n(4) Directly to:\n\na. A used oil aggregation point that is owned or operated, or both, by the same generator;\n\nb. A commercial used oil collection center that has registered with the department in accordance with Env-Hw 1406.07; or\n\nc. A facility authorized under the destination state’s rules to handle the used oil.\n\n(e) A used oil generator, household DIY used oil collection center, commercial used oil collection center, or used oil aggregation point that wishes to direct a shipment of used oil from its facility to a used oil burner shall be subject to regulation as a used oil fuel marketer under Env-Hw 1410, except as provided in Env-Hw 1410.01(b).\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25; ss by #14529, eff 2-28-26, EXPIRES: 2-28-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
}
